<!--
  Gmail filters for the operator's inbox (the address in DPDP_OPERATOR_EMAIL).

  WHAT THIS IS. The dpdp-inbound-mail Edge Function emails the operator one notice
  per incoming message ONLY for the two legal-clock classes that arrive one by one
  (GRIEVANCE and DATA REQUEST; owner decision 2026-10-01) and for a classifier failure,
  From dpdp@veridian-aios.com, with a subject that starts with the class label and the
  ticket number, for example
      [GRIEVANCE G-2026-0042] original subject
  Every other class is recorded and listed in ONE digest a day,
      [DPDP daily digest] N new tickets
  The subject formats come from supabase/functions/_shared/mail-taxonomy.ts
  (notificationSubject and CLASS_LABEL). One filter below per class that had a per-message
  notice (the other class filters stay: they cost nothing and apply to any old or hand-forwarded
  notice), one for the classifier-failure notice and one for the daily digest.

  WHAT THE FILTERS DO
    * Apply the label DPDP/Grievance, DPDP/Data request, DPDP/Review, DPDP/Sales,
      DPDP/Sales thread, DPDP/Invoice, DPDP/Monday replies, DPDP/Statutory,
      DPDP/Partner or DPDP/Support.
    * For the three legal-clock classes (GRIEVANCE, DATA REQUEST, REVIEW) also:
      star it, mark it Important, and never send it to Spam.
    * Never send it to Spam for every other class too. A notice From an address that
      is also one of your Send-mail-as aliases is exactly the kind of mail Gmail is
      quick to distrust, and a notice in Spam is a notice nobody reads.
    * NOTHING here archives, mutes, deletes or marks anything as read: there is no
      shouldArchive, shouldMarkAsRead, shouldTrash or forwardTo in this file, and a
      test (src/lib/services/dpdp-mail-edge-functions.test.ts) fails if one appears.

  LIMITS, STATED HONESTLY
    * Gmail matches a subject by WORD anywhere in it, not by "starts with", and
      ignores case and punctuation. So each filter also requires From
      dpdp@veridian-aios.com, and a notice whose original subject happens to contain
      another class word (for example "[Support H-2026-0002] invoice for partner")
      gets that class label too, and one containing grievance, review or data request
      is starred and marked Important as well. That only adds labels and stars; it
      never hides anything.
    * The Sales filter excludes the phrase "Sales thread" so the two Sales classes do
      not both label the same notice.
    * If DPDP_EMAIL_FROM is set to some other address the From condition stops
      matching and these filters do nothing; change the From value below to match.
    * Importing does not touch mail that is already in the inbox unless you tick
      "Also apply filter to matching conversations" on the import screen.

  HOW TO IMPORT (Gmail on the web, signed in as the operator)
    Settings (gear) -> See all settings -> Filters and Blocked Addresses ->
    Import filters -> Choose file (this file) -> Open file -> tick all -> Create
    filters. Gmail creates any missing DPDP/... label; if it does not, create the
    labels first under Settings -> Labels. Full walk-through:
    dpdp-app/OPERATIONS.md, section "Single mailbox".
-->
<feed xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom' xmlns:apps='http://schemas.google.com/apps/2006'>
  <title>Mail Filters</title>
  <id>tag:mail.google.com,2008:filters:dpdp-single-mailbox</id>
  <updated>2026-09-29T00:00:00Z</updated>
  <author>
    <name>VERIDIAN AI DPDP</name>
  </author>

  <!-- Legal-clock class: GRIEVANCE. Starred, Important, never Spam, never archived. -->
  <entry>
    <category term='filter'></category>
    <title>DPDP [GRIEVANCE ...]</title>
    <id>tag:mail.google.com,2008:filter:dpdp-grievance</id>
    <updated>2026-09-29T00:00:00Z</updated>
    <content></content>
    <apps:property name='from' value='dpdp@veridian-aios.com'/>
    <apps:property name='subject' value='GRIEVANCE'/>
    <apps:property name='label' value='DPDP/Grievance'/>
    <apps:property name='shouldStar' value='true'/>
    <apps:property name='shouldAlwaysMarkAsImportant' value='true'/>
    <apps:property name='shouldNeverSpam' value='true'/>
  </entry>

